        "agent": "Beacon Works",
        "kind": "communication",
        "payload": {
          "content": "Beacon Works update: The capacity constraints are tighter than expected. For my irrigation pump (8-12h, 2.4kW), even my exclusive Geothermal can't handle it (max 1.4kW at 8-9, drops to 0.6kW by 11-12). Biomass is also insufficient (1.2-1.7kW). I'm planning to: (1) Use Geothermal for my 0-6h refrigeration (0.9kW) - fits easily. (2) For 8-12h pump: will likely need to accept some overflow regardless of source choice, but Biomass seems slightly better. (3) For 18-20h refrigeration (2.9kW): Biomass capacity is 2.1-2.7kW, so minimal overflow. Cascade Labs - given your heavy 3-6 Biomass needs, I won't conflict there. Aurora - we both have timing flexibility issues in the 7-12 window. Should we coordinate who uses which source when?",
          "phase": "planning",
          "iteration": 1
        }
